WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.641
Password reset: links and support options.

2
00:00:03.641 --> 00:00:09.765
Handle expired, replaced or closed links,
locked accounts, unavailable email,

3
00:00:09.765 --> 00:00:12.392
and a missing authenticator.

4
00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.801
Reset links are private and short lived.

5
00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:22.229
This example shows the messages you
may see when a link cannot be used.

6
00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:26.522
If a link has expired,
choose Ask for a new link.

7
00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:30.056
Do not keep retrying the expired email.

8
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.909
A newer reset request
replaces the previous link.

9
00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:38.450
Use the newest email, even if
older messages arrive later.

10
00:00:38.815 --> 00:00:42.298
An invalid or incomplete
link also cannot be used.

11
00:00:42.298 --> 00:00:47.227
Open the complete link from the
newest email, or request another.

12
00:00:47.588 --> 00:00:51.485
A locked account must wait or
be unlocked by an administrator.

13
00:00:51.485 --> 00:00:55.280
A password-reset link does
not bypass an account lock.

14
00:00:55.650 --> 00:01:00.644
An account that has never enrolled an
authenticator cannot reset its password by

15
00:01:00.644 --> 00:01:01.644
email.

16
00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:04.915
Ask the administrator to
verify your identity and help.

17
00:01:05.215 --> 00:01:08.362
Too many wrong verification
codes close the link.

18
00:01:08.362 --> 00:01:13.050
Ask for a new link or contact your
administrator instead of continuing to

19
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.450
guess.

20
00:01:21.597 --> 00:01:25.474
If the app is missing but you
have an unused recovery code,

21
00:01:25.474 --> 00:01:28.825
a fresh reset link can use
it as the second factor.

22
00:01:28.825 --> 00:01:30.868
The code is then used up.

23
00:01:44.107 --> 00:01:47.320
Some MERIT installations
cannot email reset links.

24
00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:52.396
Their reset page tells you to contact an
administrator after confirming who you

25
00:01:52.396 --> 00:01:53.396
are.

26
00:01:53.408 --> 00:01:59.143
If you have lost both the password and the
authenticator, and have no recovery codes,

27
00:01:59.143 --> 00:02:03.996
contact your administrator to
verify your identity and reset both.

28
00:02:04.351 --> 00:02:05.752
Email never arrives?

29
00:02:05.752 --> 00:02:10.938
Check the user name and junk folder,
then use your agency support channel.

30
00:02:10.938 --> 00:02:15.822
The Check your email page does
not prove that an account exists.

31
00:02:16.196 --> 00:02:20.530
After a successful reset, return
to the normal sign-in process.

32
00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:25.676
Your authenticator still works unless
an administrator has reset MFA.

33
00:02:29.016 --> 00:02:33.538
In this video you recognized unusable
links and account restrictions,

34
00:02:33.538 --> 00:02:38.846
reset a password using an unused recovery
code, and identified when administrator

35
00:02:38.846 --> 00:02:40.754
assistance is required.
